%N A399969 Numbers k such that the number of divisors of k divides k + 2.
%C A399969 Numbers k such that k == -2 (mod A000005(k)).
%C A399969 Includes p^2 for every prime p except 3, 2*p for every odd prime p, and 4*p for every prime == 5 mod 6.
%H A399969 Robert Israel, <a href="/A399969/b399969.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%e A399969 a(5) = 10 is a term because 10 has 4 divisors (1, 2, 5, 10) and 4 divides 10 + 2 = 12.
%p A399969 filter:= k -> (k+2) mod NumberTheory:-tau(k) = 0:
%p A399969 select(filter, [$1..1000]);
%t A399969 Select[Range[300], Divisible[# + 2, DivisorSigma[0, #]] &] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Sep 24 2026 *)
